# API contracts

This Rule is a high-probability reminder, not a complete detector of contract changes.

Treat behavior as externally contract-relevant when it changes observable request or response semantics, including validation, status/errors, authorization or visibility, shape, filtering, ordering, pagination, cursor behavior, lifecycle meaning, or mutation effects.

Reason through the complete affected chain:

backend owner → owning tests → published contract → affected data-access/query owners → cache/state behavior → UI consumers

When an HTTP change affects the OpenAPI contract, regenerate through the established workflow:

`make schema` → `make web-api-generate`

Do not hand-edit generated API artifacts, and do not regenerate them when the OpenAPI contract is unchanged.

External semantics can change without an OpenAPI shape change. In that case, update the owning tests and affected consumers without forcing schema or client regeneration.

Published contracts under `contracts/**` keep their own ownership and validation. Do not apply the OpenAPI generation chain unless the HTTP API also changed.

Contract changes may originate outside `api/` files. Services, selectors, permissions, models, or client wrappers can change externally observable behavior even when this Rule did not attach.